The ASK meta-brand public landing site — a reference implementation of the
ASK design family.

This product vendors foundations, one pattern, three visual rules, and the
canonical browser-icon set from design-system-ASK
(github.com/apexSolarKiss/design-system-ASK):
  - colors_and_type.css        — canonical tokens (Tier 1 + Tier 2)
  - fonts/                      — Inter + JetBrains Mono variable webfonts (OFL; see fonts/*-OFL.txt)
  - assets/logo-ASK.*          — the logo-ASK wordmark (ASK Tier 3)
  - surface-shell.css          — the surface-shell pattern: the shared page
                                 shell, vendored as a pinned byte-identical
                                 copy and not modified here
  - surface-panel.css          — the shared visual contract for live content
                                 panels, vendored as a pinned byte-identical
                                 copy and not modified here. Presentation
                                 only: it owns no markup and no semantics
  - spectral-state.css         — the spectral-state primitive, vendored as a
                                 pinned byte-identical copy and not modified
                                 here. It is carried by the CFW mind map at
                                 apex-solar-kiss/consciousness-free-will/map/,
                                 which requires its governed-state custom
                                 properties
  - surface-action.css         — the shared compact-action visual contract,
                                 vendored as a pinned byte-identical copy and
                                 not modified here. It owns the base surface,
                                 foreground, border, geometry and interaction;
                                 the consuming surface keeps the element
                                 semantics, destination, copy, row and
                                 placement
  - surface-text-link.css      — the shared unboxed-textual-link contract,
                                 vendored as a pinned byte-identical copy and
                                 not modified here. It is OPT-IN BY CLASS: only
                                 an element carrying `.surface-text-link` takes
                                 it, and it is scoped to unboxed textual
                                 traversal — shaped controls, marks, figures,
                                 panels and image links are excluded. It owns
                                 rest, hover, active and focus presentation and
                                 deliberately sets NO foreground: the
                                 contextual text colour remains this site's to
                                 choose, supplied by the consuming region
  - favicon.svg, favicon-32.png,
    favicon.ico,
    apple-touch-icon.png         — the canonical ASK browser-icon set, vendored
                                 as pinned byte-identical copies and not
                                 modified here. design-system-ASK is the
                                 implementation owner; the three files this site
                                 already served remained byte-identical when that
                                 authority moved, and favicon.ico was added to
                                 answer the root probe browsers make unasked

design-system-ASK owns the shared page shell. It governs the page container,
the header layout, the wordmark slot, the structural title and lede, the header
rule, and the footer ROW — its alignment and arrangement. It does not own each
footer destination's presentation: those are compact actions, so their type,
geometry, paint and interaction belong to the action contract below. It also owns the panel
and compact-action appearance through the vendored visual rules, and the two
splits differ:

  - the panel contract governs a panel's arrangement and paint and the type
    roles of its title and supporting copy, but sets no supporting foreground —
    that value is this site's to choose;
  - the action contract governs a compact control's base surface, foreground,
    border, geometry and interaction, disclaiming none of them; this site keeps
    the element semantics, destination, copy, row and placement. One bounded
    exception is deliberate: the gallery link carries an on-image
    contextual-paint adaptation over that canonical base so it stays legible
    above a photograph.

The shell itself is Tier-3-neutral: it carries no Tier 3 value and supplies
none. This site supplies its own Tier 3 identity into the shell's mark slot and
into the browser-icon set, keeps its own markup and semantics, and adds instance-specific payload and layout
adaptations — it does not add all of its own layout, and it defines no new
tokens. It consumes the shell's optional navigation runtime:
`surface-shell.js` is vendored once at the repo root, and each shell page opts
in by authoring a navigation source. The homepage is the explicit exception: it
keeps its own composition and does not consume the shell or its runtime, though
it does consume the panel and compact-action visual rules — its footer
destinations are compact actions like every other footer on the site.

One further page is a named exception: the CFW mind map at
apex-solar-kiss/consciousness-free-will/map/ is a fixed full-viewport
interactive application, not a scrolling document, and does not consume the
shell. It carries ASK Tier 3 in its application bar and follows the
design-system interactive-diagram family grammar. The exception is specific to
that page: the CFW conclusions at apex-solar-kiss/consciousness-free-will/ are
an ordinary shell page and consume the shell and its navigation runtime, as
every other non-home content page continues to do.

When this site and design-system-ASK disagree on a foundation value, on the
shell, or on a vendored visual rule, the canonical design-system-ASK file
(itself downstream of ASK's visual-identity-system.md) wins.

